    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nSeveral subsystems need to derive a short, filesystem-safe identifier from an arbitrary path, and each reinvents it ad-hoc:\n- `'undodir'` and `swapfiles` encode the full path into a single filename.\n- the upcoming terminal state dir (#40097).\n- arbitrary plugin purposes.\n- `:connect ssh://` needs the SSH ControlPath socket name to stay under the 104-byte `sun_path` limit on macOS; today the path overflows it (#39378).\n\nThere is no shared utility for this, so each use-case picks its own encoding, with inconsistent behavior and length guarantees.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nShared utility that produces a \"slug\" from an arbitrary path. Ideally a ~~reversible two-way compression rather than a one-way hash, so the original path can be recovered~~ (useful for 'undodir', swapfiles, etc.). Some use-cases (e.g. the SSH mux socket) only need a length-bounded one-way slug, so a length bound should be supported either way.\n\nRelated but different: #32546 (plugins getting their own data/cache/log dirs). Spun off from #39378.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "concretely, `slug('path/to/thing.txt')` produces a path that looks somewhat recognizable, in the sprit of e.g. the swapfile paths:\n\n```\n%Users%foo%.claude%projects%-Users-foo--local-share-nvim-site-pack-core-opt-guh-nvim%9a53a6c5-5f0b-49f8-a5f3-cf640d769745.jsonl.swp\n%Users%foo%.config%gh%config.yml.swp\n%Users%foo%.config%nvim%init.lua.swp\n%Users%foo%.local%share%nvim%site%pack%core%opt%guh.nvim%lua%guh%util.lua.swp\n%Users%foo%.local%share%nvim%site%pack%core%opt%guh.nvim%plugin%guh.lua.swp\n```\n\nbut the paths should be abbreviated in a way that doesn't totally obfuscate them, so they stay reasonably short. \nalso seems like hyphen is more readable than ye olde `%`.\n\n```\n-Users-foo-.claude-projects--<...>--9a53a6c5-5f0b-49f8-a5f3-cf640d769745.jsonl.swp\n-Users-foo-.config-gh-config.yml.swp\n-Users-foo-.config-nvim-init.lua.swp\n-Users-foo-.local-share-nvim-<...>-lua-guh-util.lua.swp\n-Users-foo-.local-share-nvim-<...>-guh.nvim-plugin-guh.lua.swp\n```\n\n~~and ideally, the path can be \"expanded\" back into the original path. so the `<...>` part in the above paths is a compressed form that can be decompressed.~~\n\n## Proposal\n\nafter some thought, the \"reversible\" requirement conflicts with the \"short\" requirement. and we don't really need it because swap/undo/terminal-state already store the path in their metadata. so we only need readable/intuitive paths.\n\n- bounded, one-way: `slug(path, {maxlen=N})`\n    - `<readable-truncated-prefix>-<short-hash>`\n    - `-Users-foo-…-guh.lua-9a53a6c5`\n- extra readable \"compression\": a dictionary substitution of known prefixes (`$HOME`, cwd, `stdpath('data')`, plugin roots).\n- maybe we should extend the existing `pathshorten()` function?\n- edge cases:\n    - handle Windows reserved names\n    - handle case-insensitive collisions",
