            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> AFAIK What a filesystem slug really is for is to have persistent storage to store arbitrary data per file-'identity' (usually its file path).\n\nyes, and that's a useful convention (e.g. because it's intuitive for users to see which metadata maps to which files). the proposal here is intended to make it easier to do that in a reliable, consistent way.\n\nhow does this conflict with \"focus on 'underlying needs' to design the API\" ?",
