            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> how does this conflict with \"focus on 'underlying needs' to design the API\" ?\n\nI'm mostly thinking about the caller, the fact that it's implemented using a slug in the filesystem could stay an implementation detail (or a specific backend impl), but I don't think it should be part of the API to request such storage area.\n\nCompare:\n1. _I need to store arbitrary data for a file, I know one way is to get a slug of the file (impl detail), I'm asking that (I know it'll be a file) and create the file / read/write to it_\nvs\n2. _I need to store arbitrary data for a file, I call (random verbose example) `vim.storage.persistent_storage_path(\"path or bufnr or ...\", { usage = \"foo\" })` and read/write to it_\n\nThe fact that it returns a local filesystem path could even be abstracted away in some cases and return an IO primitive for writing data directly to it. 🤔",
