        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> length guarantees\n\nI haven't considered this for terminal `.mpack` files. And this can possibly fix https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/8137 and https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/16159\n\n> * extra readable \"compression\": a dictionary substitution of known prefixes (`$HOME`, cwd, `stdpath('data')`, plugin roots).\n\n~Is this for the path/fname length? If so, I think it's where \"truncate+hash\" works, rather than substituted markers. I mean, these won't save too much and the substituted markers (`~`, `$HOME`, ...) themselves can be real, user-chosen directory names. That's why the terminal state naming currently keeps the absolute path.~\n\nWell, such names are rare in practice, and since the slug is one-way, so I think it should be fine if we do so.\n \n> * maybe we should extend the existing `pathshorten()` function?\n\nI don't think so. `pathshorten()` returns a path rather than a filesystem-safe filename. It still contains separators.\n\nAlso, for future reference, if this will apply to existing subsystems, we should consider compatibility issues.",
            "created_at": "2026-07-25T17:35:23Z",
